From cdd567e4449ee69d55e6e82ecf8c2e84700e36e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reuben olinsky <reubeno@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:32:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: run resource-limit and minimum-libc cases on Python
 3.14

Origin: Azure Linux (original downstream change, not an upstream backport).

The tests in this source version select Python 3.12. This patch was
authored for Azure Linux to retain their coverage while retiring
interpreters older than Python 3.14. It is not present in the uv upstream
repository or in the Fedora commit referenced below.

Retarget the test interpreters, synthetic wheel ABI tags, and expected
snapshots together. Advance the next-minor marker split from 3.13 to 3.15
so both sides of the wheel compatibility boundary remain tested.
No production code or test assertions are removed.

Base source: uv 0.12.19, selected by the locked Fedora dist-git commit:
6311776fb745af3f8c6edfb79716c4c459d5197b
https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/uv/c/6311776fb745af3f8c6edfb79716c4c459d5197b
This reference identifies the input package only; it is not the source
of this Python 3.14 adaptation.

Upstream-Status: Not submitted

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
